WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.449
I’ve been using the Samsungs new Galaxy
buds, and I’m way more impressed than I

00:00:03.449 --> 00:00:04.449
thought they would be.

00:00:04.449 --> 00:00:08.469
I started off with the S10+, where the setup
process was familiar but less fluid than my

00:00:08.469 --> 00:00:12.200
Airpod’s, and after I was greeted with the
Galaxy wearable app that allowed me to change

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:16.460
the EQ for all audio which is something I’ve
wanted since the Airpods were released.

00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:19.630
I enjoyed using them with the Android Phone,
and that got me thinking.

00:00:19.630 --> 00:00:23.330
Are the Galaxy buds worth buying and using
as an alternative to the Airpods, if you own

00:00:23.330 --> 00:00:24.330
an iPhone?

00:00:24.330 --> 00:00:28.430
To get it right out there, Yes, I think for
a lot of iOS users the Galaxy buds may be

00:00:28.430 --> 00:00:32.290
a better buy, but not for everyone, and I’ll
tell you why in just a bit.

00:00:32.290 --> 00:00:35.739
Let's start out with the first enticement
with the buds, and that's the price.

00:00:35.739 --> 00:00:41.489
$129 isn’t that much lower than the $159
Apple charges for their super successful Airpod’s,

00:00:41.489 --> 00:00:46.149
but if you care about wireless charging that
will cost you another $40, $70 more than the

00:00:46.149 --> 00:00:48.699
Galaxy buds that come with wireless charging
built in.

00:00:48.699 --> 00:00:52.899
Not everyone cares about that, but what does
matter to all is battery life.

00:00:52.899 --> 00:00:57.440
The Galaxy buds last 6 hours instead of the
5, but the charging chase only offers 7 additional

00:00:57.440 --> 00:01:00.789
hours compared to close to 20 with the Airpods.

00:01:00.789 --> 00:01:04.710
The Cradle cases work similarly, but the Galaxy
buds is larger overall.

00:01:04.710 --> 00:01:08.900
The next enticement is the sealed design with
multiple earbud and wing tips to make sure

00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:10.940
you get a great seal and fit.

00:01:10.940 --> 00:01:13.940
Even though the AirPods fit me perfectly,
This has been the biggest complaint I’ve

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:17.191
heard about them for those who they don’t
fit and a huge reason for an iPhone user to

00:01:17.191 --> 00:01:18.940
go with the Galaxy buds.

00:01:18.940 --> 00:01:21.860
Another thing I love is the fact that they
are practically flush with my ears when I

00:01:21.860 --> 00:01:24.470
have them in, meaning I can use them with
a helmet on.

00:01:24.470 --> 00:01:27.690
The sealed design is great for a time where
you want to cut down background noise and

00:01:27.690 --> 00:01:29.620
even partially protect your hearing.

00:01:29.620 --> 00:01:32.950
If you're using an Android device you’ll
have an ambient sound feature, but since we

00:01:32.950 --> 00:01:35.790
don’t have the Galaxy wearable app in iOS
that will be missing.

00:01:35.790 --> 00:01:39.410
Along with that, you won’t have an all-around
EQ controller but the Airpods don’t have

00:01:39.410 --> 00:01:42.500
this either, instead, you can make adjustments
on an App basis.

00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:46.450
Honestly, I didn’t find that I needed to
since the default settings were my favorite

00:01:46.450 --> 00:01:48.780
out of the options Samsung gives.

00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:52.620
The highs are crisp, mids are balanced, and
the bass is worlds ahead of the AirPods thanks

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:53.860
to the sealed design.

00:01:53.860 --> 00:01:57.500
If you care about sound quality, the Galaxy
buds are definitely ahead and sound impressive

00:01:57.500 --> 00:01:58.530
for the price.

00:01:58.530 --> 00:02:03.170
So we have a lower price, wireless charging,
compact design, better sound and fit for most,

00:02:03.170 --> 00:02:07.880
and along with that an IPX2 for sweat and
light spash resistance, but what are the downsides

00:02:07.880 --> 00:02:09.530
if you use them with an iPhone?

00:02:09.530 --> 00:02:12.950
The biggest one for me is the fact that they
aren’t as seamless as the AirPods with the

00:02:12.950 --> 00:02:14.620
W1 or H1 chip.

00:02:14.620 --> 00:02:18.310
I love that the AirPods automatically get
added to all of my iCloud devices and I just

00:02:18.310 --> 00:02:20.770
open the case, put them in, and they auto
pair.

00:02:20.770 --> 00:02:23.769
You won’t get this same fluid experience
but it's still not bad.

00:02:23.769 --> 00:02:27.069
The work like any other Bluetooth headphones
so connect them once to each device and then

00:02:27.069 --> 00:02:30.319
if you want to switch from your Mac to the
iPhone go into the Bluetooth settings and

00:02:30.319 --> 00:02:33.950
manually hit connect.

00:02:33.950 --> 00:02:40.430
In the batteries widget you’ll see the battery
life but unfortunately, it's not broken down

00:02:40.430 --> 00:02:44.139
into each bud and you also can’t see the
case’s charge level like you can with the

00:02:44.139 --> 00:02:45.139
AirPods.

00:02:45.139 --> 00:02:48.489
On the plus side, you can still single tap
to pause and unpause, double tap to skip a

00:02:48.489 --> 00:02:50.680
song, and even hold down to invoke Siri.

00:02:50.680 --> 00:02:53.480
You can also use the built-in Mic’s just
like with any Bluetooth devices.

00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:56.180
Overall, I’m very impressed with the Galaxy
buds.

00:02:56.180 --> 00:02:59.650
The sound quality and feature set is fantastic
for the price and even if you’re using an

00:02:59.650 --> 00:03:03.780
iPhone they are a great option with very little
downsides compared to Apple’s offering so

00:03:03.780 --> 00:03:07.020
I can confidently say Yes they are worth it
for iPhone users.

